{"name":"Land Light","hex":"#dfcaaa","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"land","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The part of Earth which is not covered by oceans or other bodies of water.","Real estate or landed property; a partitioned and measurable area which is owned and acquired and on which buildings and structures can be built and erected."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To descend to a surface, especially from the air.","To alight, to descend from a vehicle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/land"},{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"}],"entries":[{"title":"Land","blocks":[{"text":"Land, also known as dry land, ground, or earth, is the solid terrestrial surface of Earth not submerged by the ocean or another body of water. It makes up approximately 29% of Earth's surface and includes all continents and islands. Earth's land surface is almost entirely covered by regolith, a layer of rock, soil, and minerals that forms the outer part of the crust. Land plays an important role in Earth's climate system, being involved in the carbon cycle, nitrogen cycle, and water cycle. One-third of land is covered in trees another third is used for agriculture, and roughly one-tenth is covered in glacier ice. The remainder consists of desert, savannah, and prairie."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3d/Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg/330px-Coastline_as_seen_from_Chimney_Rock%2C_Point_Reyes_National_Seashore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land","wikidata":"Q11081619"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Earth_formation.jpg/500px-Earth_formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Earth_formation.jpg/1280px-Earth_formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Earth_formation.jpg/500px-Earth_formation.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Artist's conception of Hadean Eon Earth","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEarth_formation.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Continental_models.gif/500px-Continental_models.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Continental_models.gif/1280px-Continental_models.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Continental_models.gif/500px-Continental_models.gif?utm_source=en